title: Linux VDSO Hijacking Indicators
id: 77b15184-aec5-4a6a-b69b-4deac4832179
status: experimental
description: Detects indicators of VDSO hijacking on Linux, where an attacker patches the virtual dynamic shared object of a target process to redirect syscalls to injected code, typically via ptrace against a target followed by memory writes to the vdso region.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1055/014/
logsource:
  product: linux
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - 'vdso'
      - '[vdso]'
    CommandLine|contains:
      - 'ptrace'
      - '/proc/'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - User
falsepositives:
  - Rare legitimate use
level: medium
tags:
  - attack.defense_evasion
  - attack.t1055.014
